.\" mantis(1) — keep in sync with src/index.ts when commands/options change.
.\" The cli-release workflow substitutes __MANTIS_VERSION__ with the release
.\" version before tarballing. Local builds see the literal placeholder.
.TH MANTIS 1 "May 2026" "mantis __MANTIS_VERSION__" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
mantis \- self-hostable tripwires CLI

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mantis
[\fIGLOBAL-OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mantis
is the command-line client for Mantis, a self-hostable canary / tripwire
service. It creates trigger URLs (\fIkeys\fR) that fire notifications when
accessed, inspects hits, manages notification destinations, generates
honey-file artifacts (Office docs, PDFs, SVGs, ICS, vCard, etc.), and embeds
host-event installers into systems for tamper detection.
.PP
API keys are stored in the operating-system keychain (Keychain Access on
macOS, Secret Service on Linux). Non-sensitive profile metadata lives in
.IR ~/.config/mantis/config.json .
.PP
The CLI supports multiple profiles \(em one per Mantis server \(em selectable
via
.BR \-\-profile ,
the
.B MANTIS_PROFILE
environment variable, or
.BR "mantis profile use" .

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the CLI version and exit.

.TP
.B \-\-help
Show usage. Works at every level (\fBmantis --help\fR, \fBmantis profile --help\fR,
\fBmantis edge mint --help\fR, ...).

.TP
.BI \-\-base\-url " url"
Override the stored base URL for one invocation (skips profile lookup).

.TP
.BI \-\-key " key"
Override the stored API key for one invocation.

.TP
.BI \-p " name" ", " \-\-profile " name"
Use a named profile instead of the active one. Also reads
.BR MANTIS_PROFILE .

.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON to stdout (where supported).

.TP
.BI \-\-output " mode"
Output mode for table commands:
.BR table ", " json ", or " wide .

.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress human-readable stdout. Useful in scripts.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-headers
Hide table headers.

.TP
.BI \-\-color " when"
When to colorize output:
.BR auto ", " always ", or " never .
Also honors
.BR NO_COLOR " and " FORCE_COLOR .
Default
.B auto
colors only on a TTY.

.TP
.B \-\-debug
On failure, print the resolved target, a stack trace, and HTTP request
details to stderr. Also enabled by
.BR MANTIS_DEBUG .

.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " duration"
Request timeout. Accepts forms like
.BR 500ms ", " 5s ", " 1m .

.TP
.BI \-\-retries " n"
Retry count for transient GET failures (0\-5).

.SH COMMANDS
.SS Authentication & profiles
.TP
.B mantis init
Guided first-time setup. Asks whether to use a stateful server or a stateless
edge worker, runs the matching credential flow, and (for a server) offers to
create a first key. Interactive only.

.TP
.B mantis login [\-u URL] [\-\-key\-stdin] [\-\-no\-switch]
Prompt for a Mantis server URL and API key, then store the key in the OS
keychain. Use
.B \-\-profile <name>
to save under a named profile;
.B \-\-no\-switch
keeps the current profile active;
.B \-\-key\-stdin
reads the key from stdin (leak-free, for CI) instead of prompting.

.TP
.B mantis logout [\-\-all]
Clear stored credentials for the current profile, or every profile with
.BR \-\-all .

.TP
.B mantis whoami
Show the active profile: server URL, key prefix, Cloudflare Access state,
linked mantis-edge worker.

.TP
.B "mantis profile {list,current,use,show,rm,set-edge} [args]"
Manage profiles. Each profile is a (URL, API key, optional Cloudflare Access
mode, optional default mantis-edge worker URL) tuple.

.TP
.B "mantis cloudflare {login,logout,set-service-auth,status}"
Authenticate the CLI against Cloudflare Access (SSO via the
.B cloudflared
binary, or headless Service-Auth client id / secret) for Mantis servers behind
Access.

.SS Keys: create, inspect, lifecycle
.TP
.B mantis new [memo] [opts]
Create a new key. Without
.IR memo
runs an interactive flow. Notable options:
.BR \-w / \-\-notify\-webhook ,
.BR \-e / \-\-notify\-email ,
.BR \-N / \-\-notify
.IR channel:target ,
.BR \-r / \-\-response\-kind ,
.BR \-\-expires\-at ,
.BR \-\-copy ,
.BR \-\-qr
.IR file ,
and file-artifact flags
.RB ( \-\-docx ", " \-\-xlsx ", " \-\-pptx ", " \-\-pdf ", " \-\-folder ", " \-\-svg ", " \-\-html ", " \-\-md ", " \-\-eml ", " \-\-ics ", " \-\-vcf ).

.TP
.B mantis bulk-create \-\-csv FILE \-\-out FILE [opts]
Create many keys from a CSV, writing an output CSV with generated URLs.
Aliased as
.BR "mantis import-csv" .

.TP
.B mantis list [\-n N] [\-a] [\-\-id\-only|\-\-url\-only]
List keys, most recent first. Aliased as
.BR "mantis ls" .

.TP
.B mantis show <id> [\-\-copy] [\-\-qr\-terminal] [\-\-id\-only|\-\-url\-only]
Show one key. Any
.IR id
accepts a prefix of \(>=\& 4 hex chars or the literal
.B last
(most recent key).

.TP
.B mantis last
Print the id of the most-recently-created key.

.TP
.B mantis open [id] [\-\-dashboard|\-\-trigger]
Open the key's dashboard page in the browser. No id opens the dashboard root;
.B \-\-trigger
opens the trigger URL (fires the canary).

.TP
.B "mantis disable <id> / mantis enable <id>"
Toggle a key without losing hit history.

.TP
.B mantis rm <id> [\-y]
Delete a key and cascade its hits. Aliased as
.BR "mantis delete" .

.SS Hits & monitoring
.TP
.B mantis hits <id> [opts]
Show recent hits for a key. Filters:
.BR \-\-since
.IR duration ,
.BR \-\-ip
.IR addr ,
.BR \-\-bot\-only .
Use
.BR \-f / \-\-follow
to stream live (default poll interval 3s).

.TP
.B mantis watch [id] [\-i SECONDS]
Poll across all keys (or one) and print new hits as they arrive.

.TP
.B mantis status [id] [\-w] [\-\-tripped\-only] [\-i N]
Show monitor state. Without
.IR id :
summary across all monitored keys. With
.IR id :
detail (window: hits + expiry; latch: hits since reset).
.BR \-w / \-\-watch
refreshes continuously.

.TP
.B mantis monitor <id> \-m {off,latch,window} [\-\-window SECONDS]
Configure the Uptime Kuma status endpoint for a key.

.TP
.B mantis reset <id>
Reset a key's tripped (latched) monitor state.

.SS Notifications
.TP
.B "mantis destinations {list,add,rm,test,rotate-secret} <key-id> [args]"
Incrementally manage notification destinations on a key. Channels:
.BR webhook ", " email ", " slack ", " discord ", " teams .
.B add
fires an activation ping;
.B test
fires a synthetic hit and reports which destinations succeeded.
Aliased as
.BR "mantis dest" .

.SS Audit
.TP
.B mantis audit log [opts]
Read the append-only audit log (admin keys only). Filters:
.BR \-\-since ", " \-\-type ", " \-\-actor .

.SS File artifacts
.TP
.B mantis download <id> \-\-FORMAT FILE
Download a generated honey-file artifact for an existing key. One of:
.BR \-\-docx ", " \-\-xlsx ", " \-\-pptx ", " \-\-pdf ", " \-\-folder
(zip bundle of pre-baited files),
.BR \-\-svg ", " \-\-html ", " \-\-md ", " \-\-eml ", " \-\-ics ", " \-\-vcf ", " \-\-nfc\-label
(PDF QR fallback),
.BR \-\-apple\-wallet
(signed .pkpass).

.SS Host-event installers
.TP
.B mantis install <id> \-\-type TYPE [\-o FILE]
Generate a host-install or web-embed snippet. Built-in types include
.BR shell ", " shell-sudo ", " macos-login ", " macos-boot ", " macos-wake ", " macos-network ", " linux-boot ", " linux-wake ", " linux-network ", " windows-logon ", " windows-wake ", " windows-network ", " css-background ", " js-clone-detector ", and " nfc-ndef ,
plus any plugin-contributed types. Run
.B "mantis install"
with no
.B \-\-type
to list every available type.

.SS mantis-edge (stateless Cloudflare Worker)
.TP
.B "mantis edge {keygen,set-key,delete-key,mint} [opts]"
Manage stateless mantis-edge keys (no server round-trip; pure local crypto).
.B keygen
generates an AES key,
.B set\-key
stores it in the OS keychain, and
.B mint
produces a trigger URL.

.SS Other
.TP
.B mantis doctor [\-\-public\-url URL]
Health-check CLI config, server health, auth, Cloudflare state, and split
public/private hosts.

.TP
.B mantis detect [\-\-scope user|system|all] [\-\-deep] [\-\-verbose]
Offline self-audit for mantis-style installer artifacts on the local machine.

.TP
.B "mantis completion {bash,zsh,fish}"
Print a shell completion script. The Homebrew formula already installs these in
the right paths.

.TP
.B "mantis config {list,get,set,unset,path} [key] [value]"
Get or set machine-wide defaults applied below explicit flags. Keys:
.B output
.RB ( table / json / wide )
and
.B color
.RB ( auto / always / never ).
.B mantis config path
prints the config file location.

.TP
.B "mantis plugin {add,list,remove,upgrade} [args]"
Manage CLI plugins (third-party installer types and file formats; installed
locally, never on the server). Specs accept
.IR owner/repo ", " owner/repo@v1.0.0 ", " owner/repo@<sha> ,
or a local directory.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MANTIS_PROFILE
Default profile when
.B \-\-profile
isn't supplied.
.TP
.B MANTIS_BASE_URL
Server base URL for headless use (CI, containers) when no profile is stored.
Lower precedence than an explicitly named profile, higher than the stored
current profile. Equivalent to
.BR \-\-base\-url .
.TP
.B MANTIS_API_KEY
API key for headless use, read before the OS keychain. Equivalent to
.B \-\-key
but keeps the secret out of argv (process listings, shell history).
.TP
.B MANTIS_DEBUG
When set, enables debug output on failure (resolved target, stack trace, HTTP
details). Same as
.BR \-\-debug .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR ", " FORCE_COLOR
Standard color controls.
.B NO_COLOR
disables color;
.B FORCE_COLOR
(any value but
.BR 0 )
forces it on. See also
.BR \-\-color .
.TP
.B MANTIS_ASCII
When set, use ASCII fallbacks for unicode glyphs (for legacy/non-UTF-8
terminals).

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Generic / unclassified error.
.TP
.B 2
Used only by
.BR "mantis detect" :
installer artifacts were found (grep-style).
.TP
.B 3
Usage error (bad flag or argument value).
.TP
.B 4
Authentication error (missing/invalid credentials, HTTP 401/403, no profile).
.TP
.B 5
Not found (unknown key id/prefix, HTTP 404).
.TP
.B 6
Network error (connection failed or request timed out).
.TP
.B 7
Server error (HTTP 5xx).

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mantis/config.json
Non-sensitive profile metadata (base URL, key prefix, Cloudflare Access mode).
File mode 0600.

.TP
.IR ~/.config/mantis/plugins/ ", " ~/.local/share/mantis/plugins/
Installed CLI plugins.

.TP
.I OS keychain
API keys (service
.BR mantis-cli ,
account = base URL) and Cloudflare Access Service-Auth credentials (service
.BR mantis-cli-cf ).

.TP
.I ~/.cloudflared/
Short-lived JWTs cached by the external
.B cloudflared
binary. Managed by cloudflared, not mantis.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Log in to a Mantis server and create a key with a webhook destination:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mantis login
mantis new "billing-spreadsheet" \-\-notify\-webhook https://example.com/hook \-\-copy
.EE
.RE
.PP
Tail hits live for the most-recently-created key:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mantis hits last \-\-follow
.EE
.RE
.PP
Watch monitor state across all keys, refreshing every 5s:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mantis status \-\-watch
.EE
.RE
.PP
Generate a honey-PDF and an Apple Wallet pass for the last key:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mantis new "pos-receipt" \-\-pdf decoy.pdf
mantis download last \-\-apple\-wallet decoy.pkpass
.EE
.RE
.PP
Bulk-create keys from a CSV:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mantis bulk-create \-\-csv users.csv \-\-out users-with-urls.csv \\
    \-\-memo-template "{{name}} ({{site}})" \-\-notify\-email alerts@example.com
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run the local self-audit for mantis-style installer artifacts:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mantis detect \-\-scope all \-\-deep
.EE
.RE

